{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"What is the function of the capacitor C in a buck converter?",say:'Question one. What does the capacitor do in a buck converter?',cues:{k:'Question one',q:'What does the'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 1',lv:'U',n:1,q:"What is the function of the capacitor C in a buck converter?",say:'The capacitor carries the ripple part of the inductor current, so the load gets only the steady load current. It holds the output nearly constant, with the ideal ripple shown here.',cues:{a1:'The capacitor carries',a1b:'so the load',a2:'It holds the'},al:[['C carries the ripple part of the inductor current, so the load gets only the steady Io.','a1'],['It holds Vo nearly constant; for an ideal C, ΔVo = ΔIL/(8 fs C).','a2']],vis:(c,u,b)=>`
${PE_T(310,40,'the worked example’s buck',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle'})}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),PE_T(20,84,`${PE_iL} (A)`,{fs:22,fw:800,fill:BLU})+PE_wave(PE_ccm.map(([t,i])=>[t,i-4]),70,170,26,100,BLU,5)+PE_T(60,118,'4.6',{fs:22,a:'end',fill:PE_MUT})+PE_T(60,238,'3.4',{fs:22,a:'end',fill:PE_MUT}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1b'),PE_L(70,170,590,170,PE_MUT,2,'stroke-dasharray="8 6"')+PE_T(60,178,'4',{fs:22,a:'end',fill:PE_INK})+PE_T(600,262,`${PE_IO} = 4 A goes to the load`,{fs:22,fw:800,a:'end',fill:PE_INK})+PE_T(20,306,`${PE_sb('i','C')} = ${PE_iL} − ${PE_IO} (A)`,{fs:22,fw:800,fill:GRN})+PE_L(70,380,590,380,PE_AX,2)+PE_wave(PE_ccm.map(([t,i])=>[t,i-4]),70,380,26,90,GRN,5)+PE_T(60,388,'0',{fs:22,a:'end',fill:PE_MUT})+PE_T(588,452,'±0.6 A flows in C',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'end',fill:GRN}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),PE_T(310,496,`${PE_DVO} = 1.2/(8 × 100 kHz × 220 µF) = 6.8 mV`,{fs:22,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:BLU}))}`},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A buck converter has Vs = 24 V, D = 0.6, fs = 50 kHz, L = 200 µH and Io = 2 A. Find Vo and ΔIL.",say:'Question two. A buck: twenty-four volts in, duty ratio zero point six, fifty kilohertz, two hundred microhenries, two amps. Find the output, and the ripple.',cues:{k:'Question two',q:'A buck: twenty-four'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 2',lv:'A',n:2,q:"A buck converter has Vs = 24 V, D = 0.6, fs = 50 kHz, L = 200 µH and Io = 2 A. Find Vo and ΔIL.",say:'The output is zero point six times twenty-four: fourteen point four volts. The period is twenty microseconds, so the on-time is twelve. Ripple: nine point six volts times twelve microseconds over two hundred microhenries, zero point five seven six amps.',cues:{fk:'The output is',k1:'The output is',k1b:'fourteen point four',k2:'The period is',k2b:'so the on-time',k3:'Ripple: nine point',k3b:'zero point five seven'},calc:{f:[`${PE_VO} = D·${PE_VS}`,`${PE_DIL} = (${PE_VS} − ${PE_VO})·${PE_Ton} / L`],hint:'T = 1/50 kHz; 200 µH = 200 × 10⁻⁶ H.',fk:'fk',steps:[["Output",[`${PE_VO} = 0.6 × 24`,`${PE_VO} = 14.4 V`],["k1","k1b"]],["Timing",["T = 1/50 kHz = 20 µs",`T = 20 µs,  ${PE_Ton} = 0.6 × 20 = 12 µs`],["k2","k2b"]],["Ripple",[`${PE_DIL} = (24 − 14.4) × 12 µs / 200 µH`,`${PE_DIL} = 0.576 A`],["k3","k3b"]]],live:[0,1,2]}},
{s:QZ,k:'pq',term:'Question 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"A buck converter designed for CCM at full load is run at 5 % load with the same duty ratio. What happens to Vo?",say:'Question three. A buck, designed for continuous conduction at full load, runs at five percent load, same duty ratio. What happens to the output?',cues:{k:'Question three',q:'A buck, designed'},pause:3.4},
{s:QZ,k:'pa',term:'Answer 3',lv:'N',n:3,q:"A buck converter designed for CCM at full load is run at 5 % load with the same duty ratio. What happens to Vo?",say:'At five percent load, the inductor current can reach zero before the period ends: discontinuous conduction. Then the output rises above D times the input, toward the input. So the controller must reduce D.',cues:{a1:'At five percent',a2:'Then the output',a3:'So the controller'},al:[['The inductor current may reach zero before the period ends: the converter enters DCM.','a1'],['In DCM, Vo rises above D·Vs, toward Vs.','a2'],['The controller must reduce D to hold Vo.','a3']],vis:(c,u,b)=>`
${PE_T(310,40,'the worked example’s buck, D = 0.4',{fs:24,fw:800,a:'middle'})}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a1'),PE_T(30,84,`${PE_iL} (A)`,{fs:22,fw:800,fill:PE_MUT})+PE_L(40,330,600,330,PE_AX,2)+PE_wave(PE_ccm,40,330,26,50,BLU,5)+PE_T(600,92,'full load: CCM',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'end',fill:BLU})+PE_wave(PE_dcm,40,330,26,50,RED,5)+PE_T(600,250,'5 % load: zero gaps',{fs:22,fw:800,a:'end',fill:RED})+PE_T(40,362,'0',{fs:22,a:'middle',fill:PE_MUT})+PE_T(300,362,'10 µs',{fs:22,a:'middle',fill:PE_MUT})+PE_T(560,362,'20 µs',{fs:22,a:'middle',fill:PE_MUT}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a2'),PE_T(310,420,`DCM: ${PE_VO} > D·${PE_VS} = 20 V`,{fs:26,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:RED}))}
${g('pop',tk(c,'a3'),PE_T(310,470,'fix: the controller lowers D',{fs:26,fw:800,a:'middle',fill:GRN}))}`},
{s:LS,k:'figs',term:'Your notes',title:'For your notes',say:'Your free notes are the PDF in the description. Redraw the buck\'s volt-second areas and the boost gain curve from memory.',cues:{t:'Your free notes',f:'Redraw the buck'},tags:[["Free notes for this lesson (PDF)", "link in the description"], ["In this lesson", "Buck converter; Boost converter"], ["Key terms and glossary", "at the end of the notes"]],figs:[["Buck converter", "The worked example’s buck at D = 0.4: +30 V for 4 µs, −20 V for 6 µs, so the inductor current ramps between 3.4 A and 4.6 A."], ["Boost converter", "24 V in, D = 0.6, 60 V out; with 1 Ω of winding resistance the real gain peaks at 5 at D = 0.9, then falls."]],note:"Sources your free notes draw on: Robert W. Erickson and Dragan Maksimović (Fundamentals of Power Electronics); Muhammad H. Rashid (Power Electronics: Circuits, Devices, and Applications)"},
{s:OUT,k:'outro',term:'Outro',say:`So remember: the buck gives D times the input, the boost gives the input over one minus D, and both come from volt-second balance. Next time, buck-boost and ${P('Cuk')} converters. See you there!`,cues:{f:'So remember',w1:'the buck gives',w2:'the boost gives',w3:'and both come',n:'Next time',s:'See you there'},words:[['BUCK GAIN: D','BLU','w1'],['BOOST GAIN: 1/(1 − D)','ORG','w2'],['VOLT-SECOND BALANCE','GRN','w3']],next:["NEXT TIME", "Next lesson", "Buck-boost and Cuk converters", "book"],end:'See you there!'}
